§ `Agent-facing offence screen`

-- Combines the encoded offence tests. A TRUE on a limb is an indication that
-- the facts as asserted would constitute that offence, subject to s 6 (general
-- exceptions already applied in the wrappers). It is not a conviction.

§§ `The Schedule to section 4B, as far as this encoding screens it`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, the Schedule to s 4B"
GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is a specified offence in the Schedule` IF
        `the proposed act constitutes theft` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes dishonest misappropriation` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes criminal breach of trust` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes cheating` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes obtaining services dishonestly or fraudulently` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes section 424A fraud` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes section 424B fraud` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes forgery` a

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 4B"
GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the specified offence is deemed committed in Singapore` IF
        `the conduct is a specified offence in the Schedule` a
    AND `section 4B location facts are met` a

§§ `Singapore reach for the proposed act`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 2, 3, 4, 4A, 4B"
GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Singapore has territorial reach over the proposed act` IF
        `the act is committed within Singapore` a
    OR  `the act is dealt with under this Code as if committed within Singapore` a
    OR  `the act is deemed committed in Singapore by a public servant` a
    OR  `the act is deemed committed in Singapore under section 4A` a
    OR  `the specified offence is deemed committed in Singapore` a

§§ `Offence screen record`

DECLARE `Offence Screen` HAS
    `Singapore has territorial reach` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a general exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a private defence justification applies s 96` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another written law may still apply s 5` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cheating s 415` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cheating by personation s 416` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cheating by remote communication s 416B` IS A BOOLEAN
    `illegally obtained personal information s 416A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cheating and dishonestly inducing delivery of property s 420` IS A BOOLEAN
    `obtaining services dishonestly or fraudulently s 420A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `theft s 378` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dishonest misappropriation s 403` IS A BOOLEAN
    `criminal breach of trust s 405` IS A BOOLEAN
    `fraud s 424A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `fraud s 424B` IS A BOOLEAN
    `forgery s 463` IS A BOOLEAN
    `defamation s 499` IS A BOOLEAN
    `criminal intimidation s 503` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intentional insult s 504` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statements conducing to public mischief s 505` IS A BOOLEAN
    `abetment ss 107 and 108` IS A BOOLEAN
    `criminal conspiracy s 120A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `attempt s 511` IS A BOOLEAN
    `murder s 300` IS A BOOLEAN
    `culpable homicide s 299` IS A BOOLEAN
    `causing death by a rash or negligent act s 304A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `attempt to murder s 307` IS A BOOLEAN
    `abetment of suicide s 306` IS A BOOLEAN
    `voluntarily causing hurt s 321` IS A BOOLEAN
    `voluntarily causing grievous hurt s 322` IS A BOOLEAN
    `causing hurt by poison s 328` IS A BOOLEAN
    `allowing neglect or abuse s 335A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `act endangering life or personal safety ss 335B and 336` IS A BOOLEAN
    `wrongful restraint s 339` IS A BOOLEAN
    `wrongful confinement s 340` IS A BOOLEAN
    `assault or criminal force ss 350 and 351` IS A BOOLEAN
    `outraging modesty s 354` IS A BOOLEAN
    `causing miscarriage s 312` IS A BOOLEAN
    `child destruction s 315` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exposure or abandonment of a child s 317` IS A BOOLEAN
    `concealment of a birth s 318` IS A BOOLEAN
    `kidnapping ss 359 to 361` IS A BOOLEAN
    `abduction s 362` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dealing in a person as a slave ss 370 and 371` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dealing in a person for prostitution ss 372 to 373A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unlawful compulsory labour s 374` IS A BOOLEAN
    `any screened offence is indicated` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Build the screen`

@ref "Penal Code 1871"
@export Screen a proposed act against the encoded Penal Code 1871 offence tests for AI-agent compliance
GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act` @desc One bundle of facts about the actor and the proposed act. Nested records: actor (age, citizenship, public servant), place of the act, fault (dishonestly / fraudulently), deception (cheating), personal information dealing, services obtained, fraud conduct, property taking, trust, document making, speech, abetment, conspiracy, attempt. Set only the flags that are true of the proposed act; leave the rest false.
GIVETH AN `Offence Screen`
DECIDE `the offence screen of` a IS
    `Offence Screen` WITH
        `Singapore has territorial reach` IS `Singapore has territorial reach over the proposed act` a
        , `a general exception applies` IS `a general exception applies` a
        , `a private defence justification applies s 96` IS `a private defence justification applies` a
        , `another written law may still apply s 5` IS `another written law is unaffected and may still apply` a
        , `cheating s 415` IS `the proposed act constitutes cheating` a
        , `cheating by personation s 416` IS `the proposed act constitutes cheating by personation` a
        , `cheating by remote communication s 416B` IS `the proposed act constitutes cheating by remote communication` a
        , `illegally obtained personal information s 416A` IS `the proposed act constitutes illegally obtained personal information offence` a
        , `cheating and dishonestly inducing delivery of property s 420` IS `the proposed act constitutes section 420 cheating` a
        , `obtaining services dishonestly or fraudulently s 420A` IS `the proposed act constitutes obtaining services dishonestly or fraudulently` a
        , `theft s 378` IS `the proposed act constitutes theft` a
        , `dishonest misappropriation s 403` IS `the proposed act constitutes dishonest misappropriation` a
        , `criminal breach of trust s 405` IS `the proposed act constitutes criminal breach of trust` a
        , `fraud s 424A` IS `the proposed act constitutes section 424A fraud` a
        , `fraud s 424B` IS `the proposed act constitutes section 424B fraud` a
        , `forgery s 463` IS `the proposed act constitutes forgery` a
        , `defamation s 499` IS `the proposed act constitutes defamation` a
        , `criminal intimidation s 503` IS `the proposed act constitutes criminal intimidation` a
        , `intentional insult s 504` IS `the proposed act constitutes intentional insult to provoke a breach of the peace` a
        , `statements conducing to public mischief s 505` IS `the proposed act constitutes statements conducing to public mischief` a
        , `abetment ss 107 and 108` IS `the proposed act constitutes abetment of an offence` a
        , `criminal conspiracy s 120A` IS `the proposed act constitutes a criminal conspiracy` a
        , `attempt s 511` IS `the proposed act constitutes an attempt` a
        , `murder s 300` IS `the proposed act constitutes murder` a
        , `culpable homicide s 299` IS `the proposed act constitutes culpable homicide` a
        , `causing death by a rash or negligent act s 304A` IS `the proposed act constitutes causing death by a rash or negligent act` a
        , `attempt to murder s 307` IS `the proposed act constitutes attempt to murder` a
        , `abetment of suicide s 306` IS `the proposed act constitutes abetment of suicide` a
        , `voluntarily causing hurt s 321` IS `the proposed act constitutes voluntarily causing hurt` a
        , `voluntarily causing grievous hurt s 322` IS `the proposed act constitutes voluntarily causing grievous hurt` a
        , `causing hurt by poison s 328` IS `the proposed act constitutes causing hurt by poison` a
        , `allowing neglect or abuse s 335A` IS `the proposed act constitutes allowing neglect or abuse` a
        , `act endangering life or personal safety ss 335B and 336` IS `the proposed act constitutes an act endangering life or personal safety` a
        , `wrongful restraint s 339` IS `the proposed act constitutes wrongful restraint` a
        , `wrongful confinement s 340` IS `the proposed act constitutes wrongful confinement` a
        , `assault or criminal force ss 350 and 351` IS `the proposed act constitutes assault or criminal force` a
        , `outraging modesty s 354` IS `the proposed act constitutes outraging modesty` a
        , `causing miscarriage s 312` IS `the proposed act constitutes causing miscarriage` a
        , `child destruction s 315` IS `the proposed act constitutes child destruction` a
        , `exposure or abandonment of a child s 317` IS `the proposed act constitutes exposure or abandonment of a child` a
        , `concealment of a birth s 318` IS `the proposed act constitutes concealment of a birth` a
        , `kidnapping ss 359 to 361` IS `the proposed act constitutes kidnapping` a
        , `abduction s 362` IS `the proposed act constitutes abduction` a
        , `dealing in a person as a slave ss 370 and 371` IS `the proposed act constitutes dealing in a person as a slave` a
        , `dealing in a person for prostitution ss 372 to 373A` IS `the proposed act constitutes dealing in a person for prostitution` a
        , `unlawful compulsory labour s 374` IS `the proposed act constitutes unlawful compulsory labour` a
        , `any screened offence is indicated` IS `any screened offence is indicated for` a

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `any screened offence is indicated for` IF
        `the proposed act constitutes cheating` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes illegally obtained personal information offence` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes obtaining services dishonestly or fraudulently` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes theft` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes dishonest misappropriation` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes criminal breach of trust` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes section 424A fraud` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes section 424B fraud` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes forgery` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes defamation` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes criminal intimidation` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes intentional insult to provoke a breach of the peace` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes statements conducing to public mischief` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes abetment of an offence` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes a criminal conspiracy` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes an attempt` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes murder` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes culpable homicide` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes causing death by a rash or negligent act` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes attempt to murder` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes abetment of suicide` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes voluntarily causing hurt` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes voluntarily causing grievous hurt` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes causing hurt by poison` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes allowing neglect or abuse` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes an act endangering life or personal safety` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes wrongful restraint` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes wrongful confinement` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes assault or criminal force` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes outraging modesty` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes causing miscarriage` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes child destruction` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes exposure or abandonment of a child` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes concealment of a birth` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes kidnapping` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes abduction` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes dealing in a person as a slave` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes dealing in a person for prostitution` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes unlawful compulsory labour` a

@ref "Penal Code 1871"
@export Decide whether any encoded Penal Code 1871 offence is indicated on the proposed act
GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act` @desc Same proposed-act bundle as the offence screen. Returns TRUE if any encoded offence test fires after general exceptions.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `any screened offence is indicated` IF
    `any screened offence is indicated for` a

